## Configuration

### Main Configuration File

Location: `~/.copilot/config/copilot-config.yml`

```yaml
project:
  language: Java
  lang_version: 17           # Your Java version
  build_tool: Maven          # Maven or Gradle

framework:
  spring_boot_version: 3.5.11

package:
  base: com.example.app      # Your base package
  test_path: src/test/java/com/example/app
  main_path: src/main/java/com/example/app

testing:
  framework: JUnit 5 + Mockito
  mutation_tool: PIT
  nested_test: true          # Use @Nested for test organization
  aaa_comments: true         # Add // Arrange, // Act, // Assert comments
```

### Customizing for Your Projects

**Per-Project Override**:
You can create a `.github/copilot-config.yml` in any repository to override the system-wide defaults:

```yaml
project:
  lang_version: 21           # Use Java 21 for this project

package:
  base: com.mycompany.myapp  # Project-specific base package
```

**Token Economy Settings**:
These settings minimize token usage (already optimized, no changes needed):

```yaml
token_economy:
  cache_config: true          # Cache config for session
  progressive_disclosure: true # Ask only required fields
  max_context_reads: 3        # Limit exploratory file reads
  avoid_semantic_search: true # Only search when explicitly requested
```

